From 398f988795db6da7cb9a043c2c17ada61b20bc68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mir: the optimiser's lvalue visitor and the validator see
 borrow call parameters

webrtc-sctp 0.13.0 (localsend-cli 1.18.2, tokio 1.53.1) src/timer/ack_timer.rs:34,
the `tokio::spawn(async move { .. })` block of AckTimer<T>::start:

    tokio::select! {
        _ = timer.as_mut() => {
            if let Some(observer) = timeout_observer.upgrade() {
                let mut observer = observer.lock().await;
                observer.on_ack_timeout().await;
            }
        }
        _ = close_rx.recv() => {},
    }

    MIR ERROR: <future#I_start_182<AssociationInternal> as Future>::poll
      BB11/2: ensure_valid: Use of non-valid lvalue - a1*

`a1` is the generated poll's `cx`.  The `.await` lowering hands `&mut *cx` to
the awaited `poll` as a borrow call parameter (Param::Borrow, 0130).
mir/optimise.cpp has its own lvalue visitor family, and its Param case only
knew LValue parameters, so every optimisation pass built on it was blind to
those borrows.  Here core's `PollFn::poll` (the `select!` closure's driver)
had been inlined before monomorphisation, leaving `_n = &mut *cx; (f)(_n)`;
the reborrow elimination (MIR_Optimise_DeTemporary_ReborrowOfUnused) found
no other use of `cx` - the two later awaits only mention it in borrow
parameters - and rewrote the call to `(f)(cx)`, a move of the coroutine's
`cx`.  The validator's move_val(Param) had the same blind spot, so nothing
complained until the post-monomorphisation inlining of core's
`impl Future for Pin<Box<dyn Future>>` turned one of the later borrow
parameters into the statement `_50 = &mut *a1`.

The visitor now reports a borrow parameter's lvalue as a Borrow use, and the
validator checks that a borrowed parameter is valid.

Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5.1
---

diff --git a/src/mir/check.cpp b/src/mir/check.cpp
index 01d3a149..f26365e4 100644
--- a/src/mir/check.cpp
+++ b/src/mir/check.cpp
@@ -348,6 +348,11 @@ void MIR_Validate_ValState(::MIR::TypeResolve& state, const ::MIR::Function& fcn
             {
                 move_val(state, *e);
             }
+            else if( const auto* e = p.opt_Borrow() )
+            {
+                // The borrowed value has to be valid (it isn't moved)
+                ensure_valid(state, e->val);
+            }
         }
     private:
         static bool merge_state(State& a, State b)
diff --git a/src/mir/optimise.cpp b/src/mir/optimise.cpp
index f393504d..f8fee394 100644
--- a/src/mir/optimise.cpp
+++ b/src/mir/optimise.cpp
@@ -508,6 +508,15 @@ namespace
         {
             return visit_mir_lvalue_raw_mut(*e, u, cb);
         }
+        else if( auto* e = p.opt_Borrow() )
+        {
+            // A borrow parameter (`&mut *cx`, passed straight to `Future::poll` by the `.await` lowering) borrows its
+            // lvalue: a use of the root that must be seen by every pass. Skipped, `cx` looked unused to the
+            // reborrow elimination, which turned the inlined `PollFn::poll`'s `_n = &mut *cx; (f)(_n)` into
+            // `(f)(cx)`, moving the coroutine's `cx` (webrtc-sctp 0.13.0 timer/ack_timer.rs `select!` + two more
+            // awaits: "Use of non-valid lvalue - a1*" once a later await's poll was inlined after monomorphisation).
+            return visit_mir_lvalue_raw_mut(e->val, ValUsage::Borrow, cb);
+        }
         else
         {
             return false;
